    Derive a configured stage list with its failing point
    
    The trusted planner now derives a complete stage list from the public
    configuration: the first stage plus one choice per further stage, where the
    last choice must be the single-row stage and every other choice is a middle
    stage with one or more folded rows and at most as many mask bits. Each stage's
    capacities and random tail follow the stage rules, and every stage's code
    lengths must hold the message and its tail. A configuration the rules reject
    reports its stage and the failing point instead of a generic error. Unit tests
    cover a valid chain, both stage-shape rules, an indivisible cut and a code
    length that does not fit.
    
    The shared and own groups are still solved separately, the capacity mapping
    and the whole-chain round budget remain the next steps.

